{"title":"Questions that are rarely asked","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/910152440/0/marginalrevolution~Questions-that-are-rarely-asked.html","date":1735542590000,"content":"<p>“Which do you think is the best symphony which you never have heard?”</p>\r\n<p>It used to be the first two symphonies of Carl Nielsen, but yesterday I heard them.  They are good, probably not great, but in any case I never had heard them before.  I have heard more Haydn symphonies than you might think (all of them), so for me the answer is not one of those.</p>\r\n<p>Perhaps now it is something by Lutoslawski?  I only know two of them, and I like them.  What else does this margin hold?  And how long will I need to explore it?</p>\r\n<p>This question gets at two issues.  First, how do you assess matters you do not really know?  What kinds of evidence do you bring to bear on answering this question?</p>\r\n<p>Second, why do you stop at one margin rather than another?  <em>Why</em> don’t you know whatever you think is the best symphony you have never heard?  Was your last attempt in that direction such a miserable failure?  Are symphonies really so bad?  I think not.  No matter who you are, there are still some good ones.</p>\r\n<p>So what is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Lutoslawski-Symphonies-Witold/dp/B00AK3X3M4/ref=sr_1_1?crid=1PEK3WGIVO0GU&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.SQnTvQWwqpYE6Lhy_ibL2Ol1g4DJd4p6F3_zMpOtTtuIIven-Y_t4DVgLLuTwn_QV7eZyUtOE1IaU_Xlf1FxupxmkeTK3upTyDdiBhZtdUryhkTTxV82op9NhQCO8iReUR1Kcksu57VfQcrfVWpset--1FNkqik-GpbuUiORItbc6KTAnwf9biiCw6XHUu1on40zGQY_y3qXsEUQZ41qr61RnY-wOSqCGCqBkCK0MBM.Cziq4UXZZ-4NVNAIfmUK5VqvUtLqjZiqk7cL6QmGC9Y&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=lutoslawski+symphony&amp;qid=1735502843&amp;sprefix=lutoslawski+symphony%2Caps%2C108&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">stopping you</a>?</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2024/12/questions-that-are-rarely-asked-22.html\">Questions that are rarely asked</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/910152440/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/910152440/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/910152440/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/910152440/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/19/910152440/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/email20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/20/910152440/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/rss20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2024/12/questions-that-are-rarely-asked-22.html#comments\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/comments20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2024/12/questions-that-are-rarely-asked-22.html/feed\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/commentsrss20.png\" /></a> \r\n<div><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2024/12/questions-that-are-rarely-asked-22.html#comments\"><h3>Comments</h3></a><ul><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2024/12/questions-that-are-rarely-asked-22.html#comment-160852806\">In reply to Dana Gioia.   Thanks for the recommendation, I just ...</a> <i>by efim polenov</i></li><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2024/12/questions-that-are-rarely-asked-22.html#comm